VeridianOS: region_language: map rows to settings without LC_ADDRESS

GCC reported -Wswitch in LocaleListModel::data() and OptionsModel::data():
the enumerators Address, NameStyle and PhoneNumbers were not handled. They
are handled only under #ifdef LC_ADDRESS, which musl does not define.

LocaleListModel: without LC_ADDRESS there is no address/name/phone example;
the three enumerators are now listed in the #else branch and give no
example, which is what the switch fell through to before.

OptionsModel: this one hides a real bug on C libraries without LC_ADDRESS.
m_staticNames (the model rows) leaves out the Address, Name Style and Phone
Numbers rows there, but data() turned the row number into the setting with
static_cast<SettingType>(row). The last row, "Data and Storage Sizes", is
row 6 then, which is SettingType::Address, so its example
(m_binaryDialectExample) was never shown. setBinaryDialect() likewise
emitted dataChanged() for row SettingType::BinaryDialect (9) of a 7-row
model, so the row never refreshed. data() now reads the setting from
m_staticNames.at(row).second, as the Page role already did, and
setBinaryDialect() uses the last row, where that entry is always appended.
The three enumerators get #else cases that cannot be reached because those
rows do not exist.

On glibc (LC_ADDRESS defined) rows and settings coincide, so behaviour there
is unchanged.

--- a/kcms/region_language/localelistmodel.cpp	2026-10-08 16:59:33.579720900 -0400
+++ b/kcms/region_language/localelistmodel.cpp	2026-10-08 17:06:14.029200995 -0400
@@ -173,6 +173,12 @@
             return Utility::nameStyleExample(data.locale);
         case PhoneNumbers:
             return Utility::phoneNumbersExample(data.locale);
+#else
+        case Address:
+        case NameStyle:
+        case PhoneNumbers:
+            // The C library has no LC_ADDRESS/LC_NAME/LC_TELEPHONE: no example to show.
+            break;
 #endif
         case BinaryDialect:
             Q_ASSERT(false);
